earGradient><linearGradient id="kp-grad-line" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="70" y1="0" x2="470" y2="0"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#3D7BFF"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#8B5CF6"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#FF3D8B"/></linearGradient></defs></svg><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="nav"><nav class="nav__inner" aria-label="Main"><a class="nav__brand" href="/"><span class="logo" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><rect width="64" height="64" rx="16" fill="url(#kp-grad-v)"/><path d="M12 22C26 22 30 32 38 32M12 42C26 42 30 32 38 32" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-opacity=".7" stroke-width="3.5"/><path d="M38 32H52" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="5.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span><span>Kevin Park</span></a><div class="nav__links"><a href="/#work">Work</a><a href="/#about" data-nav="about">About</a><a href="/#experience" data-nav="experience">Experience</a><div class="tools" data-tools><button class="tools__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tools-menu">Tools<svg class="icon tools__caret" viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"/></svg></button><div class="tools__panel" id="tools-menu" hidden><p class="sr-only">Tools menu</p><ul class="tools__list"><li><a class="tools__item" href="/tools/financial-planner/"><span class="tools__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon " viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M80,120h96a8,8,0,0,0,8-8V64a8,8,0,0,0-8-8H80a8,8,0,0,0-8,8v48A8,8,0,0,0,80,120Zm8-48h80v32H88ZM200,24H56A16,16,0,0,0,40,40V216a16,16,0,0,0,16,16H200a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V40A16,16,0,0,0,200,24Zm0,192H56V40H200ZM100,148a12,12,0,1,1-12-12A12,12,0,0,1,100,148Zm40,0a12,12,0,1,1-12-12A12,12,0,0,1,140,148Zm40,0a12,12,0,1,1-12-12A12,12,0,0,1,180,148Zm-80,40a12,12,0,1,1-12-12A12,12,0,0,1,100,188Zm40,0a12,12,0,1,1-12-12A12,12,0,0,1,140,188Zm40,0a12,12,0,1,1-12-12A12,12,0,0,1,180,188Z"/></svg></span><span class="tools__text"><span class="tools__title">Financial planner</span><span class="tools__desc">A starter money plan in about 10 minutes</span></span></a></li></ul></div></div></div><a class="btn btn--blue btn--compact" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kevinswpark" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon icon--brand" viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M216,24H40A16,16,0,0,0,24,40V216a16,16,0,0,0,16,16H216a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V40A16,16,0,0,0,216,24Zm0,192H40V40H216V216ZM96,112v64a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V112a8,8,0,0,1,16,0Zm88,28v36a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V140a20,20,0,0,0-40,0v36a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V112a8,8,0,0,1,15.79-1.78A36,36,0,0,1,184,140ZM100,84A12,12,0,1,1,88,72,12,12,0,0,1,100,84Z"/></svg><span class="btn__text">Connect on LinkedIn</span><svg class="icon icon--out" viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M200,64V168a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V83.31L69.66,197.66a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L172.69,72H88a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H192A8,8,0,0,1,200,64Z"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></nav></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="progress" aria-hidden="true"></div><header class="art-head"><div class="band band--article" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="wrap art-head__in"><a class="crumb" href="/#work"><svg class="icon " viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M224,128a8,8,0,0,1-8,8H59.31l58.35,58.34a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,11.32l-72-72a8,8,0,0,1,0-11.32l72-72a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32L59.31,120H216A8,8,0,0,1,224,128Z"/></svg>All work</a><h1 id="title" tabindex="-1">Using a visual metaphor to explain ZBD’s role</h1><p class="deck">How I developed “The Money Layer for Games” to explain ZBD’s role between games and financial services.</p><ul class="facts"><li><span class="facts__k">Company</span><span class="facts__v">ZBD</span></li><li><span class="facts__k">Role</span><span class="facts__v">Senior Product Marketing Manager</span></li></ul></div></header><div class="art wrap"><aside class="rail" aria-label="On this page"><div class="rail__inner"><p class="rail__h">On this page</p><ol><li><a href="/work/money-layer/#stuck" data-target="stuck">Where money gets stuck</a></li><li><a href="/work/money-layer/#layer" data-target="layer">From a barrier to a layer</a></li><li><a href="/work/money-layer/#line" data-target="line">The line and the framework</a></li><li><a href="/work/money-layer/#learned" data-target="learned">What I learned</a></li></ol></div></aside><div class="flow"><section class="tldr" aria-labelledby="tldr-h"><h2 id="tldr-h">TL;DR</h2><dl><div><dt>Challenge</dt><dd>Explain ZBD’s role between game economies and financial systems.</dd></div><div><dt>Approach</dt><dd>Use a visual metaphor to understand the gap before naming it.</dd></div><div><dt>Output</dt><dd>“The Money Layer for Games” and the ZBD Platform messaging framework.</dd></div></dl></section><h2 id="stuck">Where money gets stuck</h2><p class="prose">In games, players can earn or buy items and currencies that have value within the game. Transferring that value to someone else or cashing it out can be difficult, so some trades happen through barter or off-platform arrangements. ZBD was building financial infrastructure to support money movement in games.</p><p class="prose">For a studio, adding these capabilities raises three issues:</p><ul class="issues"><li><span class="issues__k">Regulation:</span> Handling player funds can trigger different requirements across markets, including licenses.</li><li><span class="issues__k">Game economy:</span> Transfers and cash-out could change how an existing economy works.</li><li><span class="issues__k">Priorities:</span> A new title or feature may offer a faster return than building financial infrastructure.</li></ul><p class="prose">ZBD offered infrastructure that would be costly for studios to build themselves. I needed a clear way to explain its role.</p><h2 id="layer">From a barrier to a layer</h2><p class="prose">Every draft that tried to carry both the problem and ZBD’s ambition picked up another clause. I stepped away from the copy and pictured an Eva pushing against an AT Field in <i>Evangelion</i>.</p><figure class="fig" data-title="Concept diagram"><div class="panel fig__panel"><div class="dg-pair" role="img" aria-label="Two states of one diagram. First, a wall stops value moving from a game economy to financial systems. Second, the wall opens into a layer marked ZBD that value can cross."><div class="dg-state"><svg viewBox="0 0 560 350" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><text class="dg-label" x="30" y="44">Game economy</text><text class="dg-label" x="530" y="44" text-anchor="end">Financial systems</text><g class="dg-tokens"><circle cx="78" cy="118" r="11"/><circle cx="118" cy="186" r="11"/><circle cx="70" cy="252" r="11"/><rect x="150" y="106" width="20" height="20" rx="3" transform="rotate(45 160 116)"/><rect x="160" y="232" width="20" height="20" rx="3" transform="rotate(45 170 242)"/></g><g class="dg-accounts"><rect x="404" y="98" width="70" height="42" rx="8"/><rect x="404" y="166" width="70" height="42" rx="8"/><rect x="404" y="234" width="70" height="42" rx="8"/><path d="M404 111h70M404 179h70M404 247h70"/></g><rect class="dg-wall" x="264" y="70" width="32" height="228" rx="10"/><path class="dg-flow dg-flow--blocked" d="M92 118H250"/><path class="dg-stop" d="M255 108v20"/><path class="dg-flow dg-flow--blocked" d="M132 186H250"/><path class="dg-stop" d="M255 176v20"/><path class="dg-flow dg-flow--blocked" d="M84 252H250"/><path class="dg-stop" d="M255 242v20"/></svg><p class="dg-state__cap"><span class="dot dot--stop"></span>A boundary that blocks passage</p></div><div class="dg-state"><svg viewBox="0 0 560 350" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><text class="dg-label" x="30" y="44">Game economy</text><text class="dg-label" x="530" y="44" text-anchor="end">Financial systems</text><g class="dg-tokens"><circle cx="78" cy="118" r="11"/><circle cx="118" cy="186" r="11"/><circle cx="70" cy="252" r="11"/><rect x="150" y="106" width="20" height="20" rx="3" transform="rotate(45 160 116)"/><rect x="160" y="232" width="20" height="20" rx="3" transform="rotate(45 170 242)"/></g><g class="dg-accounts"><rect x="404" y="98" width="70" height="42" rx="8"/><rect x="404" y="166" width="70" height="42" rx="8"/><rect x="404" y="234" width="70" height="42" rx="8"/><path d="M404 111h70M404 179h70M404 247h70"/></g><g class="dg-layer"><rect x="264" y="70" width="32" height="30" rx="8"/><rect x="264" y="138" width="32" height="30" rx="8"/><rect x="264" y="206" width="32" height="30" rx="8"/><rect x="264" y="268" width="32" height="30" rx="8"/></g><text class="dg-label dg-label--layer" x="280" y="336" text-anchor="middle">ZBD</text><path class="dg-flow dg-flow--open" d="M92 118C200 118 230 119 280 119S360 118 394 118"/><path class="dg-head" d="M400.0 118.0l-8.0 -5.0v9.9z"/><path class="dg-flow dg-flow--open" d="M132 186C200 186 230 187 280 187S360 186 394 186"/><path class="dg-head" d="M400.0 186.0l-8.0 -5.0v9.9z"/><path class="dg-flow dg-flow--open" d="M84 252C200 252 230 252 280 252S360 252 394 252"/><path class="dg-head" d="M400.0 252.0l-8.0 -5.0v9.9z"/></svg><p class="dg-state__cap"><span class="dot dot--go"></span>A layer that lets value cross</p></div></div><button class="zoom-btn" type="button" data-zoom aria-label="Enlarge diagram"><svg class="icon " viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M152,112a8,8,0,0,1-8,8H120v24a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V120H80a8,8,0,0,1,0-16h24V80a8,8,0,0,1,16,0v24h24A8,8,0,0,1,152,112Zm77.66,117.66a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-50.06-50.07a88.11,88.11,0,1,1,11.31-11.31l50.07,50.06A8,8,0,0,1,229.66,229.66ZM112,184a72,72,0,1,0-72-72A72.08,72.08,0,0,0,112,184Z"/></svg></button></div><figcaption><span class="pill">Concept diagram</span>Drawn for this site.</figcaption></figure><p class="prose">The AT Field was a layer that blocked passage between two spaces. Pushing harder would not get the Eva through, which made me think about the boundary itself. I pictured ZBD in a similar position between a game’s economy and the financial world, with infrastructure that could let value move across it.</p><h2 id="line">The line and the framework</h2><p class="prose">I used that image to develop “The Money Layer for Games.” The phrase described ZBD’s role across its products.</p><figure class="fig"><div class="fig__panel fig__panel--grad"><p class="specimen">The Money Layer for Games</p></div><figcaption><span class="pill">Final work</span><a class="fig__cta" href="https://zbdpay.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on zbdpay.com<svg class="icon " viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M200,64V168a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V83.31L69.66,197.66a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L172.69,72H88a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H192A8,8,0,0,1,200,64Z"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></figcaption></figure><p class="prose">I shared the concept with leadership and the marketing team, then developed the ZBD Platform messaging framework around it.</p><p class="prose">The work also supported ZBD’s Series C fundraising, which closed in January 2026. “The Money Layer for Games” and the broader branding work contributed to how the company presented itself as it raised its next round.</p><figure class="fig"><div class="panel fig__panel fig__panel--proof"><a class="proof__host" href="https://zbdpay.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="proof__dot"></span>zbdpay.com<svg class="icon " viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M200,64V168a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V83.31L69.66,197.66a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L172.69,72H88a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H192A8,8,0,0,1,200,64Z"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><dl class="proof"><div><dt>Homepage headline</dt><dd>The Money Layer for Games.</dd></div><div><dt>Page title</dt><dd>ZBD - The Money Layer for Games</dd></div><div><dt>Meta description</dt><dd>ZBD is the money layer for games, the licensed financial infrastructure that turns money movement into a driver of engagement, revenue, and loyalty.</dd></div></dl></div><figcaption><span class="pill">Published on zbdpay.com</span>ZBD uses the line on its public website.</figcaption></figure><h2 id="learned">What I learned</h2><p class="pull">I had been trying to find the right words before I could see the relationship. Once I pictured the barrier and the layer that could bridge it, the line followed.</p></div></div><section class="next wrap" aria-labelledby="next-h"><h2 class="h2 h2--sm" id="next-h">Next case study</h2><article class="tile tile--lc tile--compact" aria-labelledby="tile-lc"><div class="tile__text"><h3 id="tile-lc"><a href="/work/money-lifecycle/">The Money Lifecycle</a></h3><p class="tile__desc">Explaining how ZBD’s products work together by following money into, through, and out of a game.</p><p class="result result--row"><span class="result__chip">Money In</span><span class="result__chip">Money Through</span><span class="result__chip">Money Out</span></p><p class="tile__impact">Used in ZBD’s messaging framework, sales decks, and public website.</p><span class="tile__go" aria-hidden="true">Read the case study<svg class="icon " viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z"/></svg></span></div><div class="tile__art"><svg class="dg-lc" viewBox="-30 0 580 360" role="img" aria-label="A loop with three stages, Money In, Money Through, and Money Out, connected by arrows."><circle class="dg-ring" cx="260" cy="176" r="82"/><path class="dg-arc" d="M292.5 62.6A118 118 0 0 1 374.5 204.5"/><path class="dg-head dg-head--arc" d="M374.0 206.5L371.1 193.4L382.7 196.3z"/><path class="dg-arc" d="M342.0 260.9A118 118 0 0 1 178.0 260.9"/><path class="dg-head dg-head--arc" d="M176.6 259.5L189.4 263.5L181.1 272.1z"/><path class="dg-arc" d="M145.5 204.5A118 118 0 0 1 227.5 62.6"/><path class="dg-head dg-head--arc" d="M229.4 62.0L219.5 71.1L216.2 59.6z"/><circle class="dg-node" cx="260.0" cy="58.0" r="8"/><text class="dg-label dg-label--stage" x="260.0" y="28.0" text-anchor="middle">Money In</text><circle class="dg-node" cx="362.2" cy="235.0" r="8"/><text class="dg-label dg-label--stage" x="378.7" y="264.0" text-anchor="start">Money Through</text><circle class="dg-node" cx="157.8" cy="235.0" r="8"/><text class="dg-label dg-label--stage" x="141.3" y="264.0" text-anchor="end">Money Out</text></svg></div></article></section><section class="closing wrap" aria-labelledby="closing"><div class="closing__card"><span class="closing__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 class="closing__h" id="closing">Let’s talk.</h2><a class="btn btn--white" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kevinswpark" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><svg class="icon icon--brand" viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M216,24H40A16,16,0,0,0,24,40V216a16,16,0,0,0,16,16H216a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V40A16,16,0,0,0,216,24Zm0,192H40V40H216V216ZM96,112v64a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V112a8,8,0,0,1,16,0Zm88,28v36a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V140a20,20,0,0,0-40,0v36a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V112a8,8,0,0,1,15.79-1.78A36,36,0,0,1,184,140ZM100,84A12,12,0,1,1,88,72,12,12,0,0,1,100,84Z"/></svg><span class="btn__text">Connect on LinkedIn</span><svg class="icon icon--out" viewBox="0 0 256 256" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M200,64V168a8,8,0,0,1-16,0V83.31L69.66,197.66a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L172.69,72H88a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H192A8,8,0,0,1,200,64Z"/></svg><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></section></main><footer class="foot wrap"><div class="foot__row"><span cla